{
  "_how_to": [
    "Maps each queue to the EC2 instances that process it. Queue names aren't case-sensitive.",
    "ec2_name: the instance Name tag (* wildcards allowed, or a list of names).",
    "env: prod-na, prod-na-2, prod-eu or prod-ca. Picks the AWS account/region, and only counts instances",
    "  tagged with that environment (prodna / prodna2 etc.), so NA and NA2 boxes with the same Name are kept apart.",
    "  Add \"match_env_tag\": false to an entry to count by Name only.",
    "Or map to Auto Scaling Groups instead:  \"<queue name>\": {\"asg\": [\"<asg name>\"]}",
    "Run: python3 sqs_monitor.py boxes   to check every queue's count.",
    "Keys starting with _ are ignored."
  ],
